[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (D) at (0,0);
\coordinate (E) at (2.9,0);
\coordinate (F) at (2.526,2.12);
\draw (D) -- (E);
\draw (E) -- (F);
\draw (F) -- (D);
\node at (0.80,0.29) {$40^{\circ}$};
\node at (2.33,0.48) {$80^{\circ}$};
\node at (2.25,1.37) {$60^{\circ}$};
\node[below left] at (D) {$D$};
\node[below right] at (E) {$E$};
\node[above] at (F) {$F$};
\coordinate (G) at (4.1,0);
\coordinate (H) at (7,0);
\coordinate (I) at (5.046,1.639);
\draw (G) -- (H);
\draw (H) -- (I);
\draw (I) -- (G);
\node at (4.79,0.40) {$60^{\circ}$};
\node at (6.15,0.31) {$40^{\circ}$};
\node at (5.18,0.90) {$80^{\circ}$};
\node[below left] at (G) {$G$};
\node[below right] at (H) {$H$};
\node[above] at (I) {$I$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The two triangles are similar. Which similarity statement is correct?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (W) at (0,0);
\coordinate (X) at (2.8,0);
\coordinate (Y) at (1.9,1.5);
\coordinate (Z) at (0,1.5);
\draw (W) -- (X) -- (Y) -- (Z) -- cycle;
\coordinate (wa) at ($(W)!0.25cm!(X)$);
\coordinate (wb) at ($(W)!0.25cm!(Z)$);
\draw (wa) -- ($(wa)+(wb)-(W)$) -- (wb);
\coordinate (za) at ($(Z)!0.25cm!(W)$);
\coordinate (zb) at ($(Z)!0.25cm!(Y)$);
\draw (za) -- ($(za)+(zb)-(Z)$) -- (zb);
\node[below left] at (W) {$W$};
\node[below right] at (X) {$X$};
\node[above right] at (Y) {$Y$};
\node[above left] at (Z) {$Z$};
\coordinate (K) at (4.6,3.4);
\coordinate (L) at (4.6,0.04);
\coordinate (M) at (6.4,1.12);
\coordinate (J) at (6.4,3.4);
\draw (K) -- (L) -- (M) -- (J) -- cycle;
\coordinate (ka) at ($(K)!0.25cm!(L)$);
\coordinate (kb) at ($(K)!0.25cm!(J)$);
\draw (ka) -- ($(ka)+(kb)-(K)$) -- (kb);
\coordinate (ja) at ($(J)!0.25cm!(K)$);
\coordinate (jb) at ($(J)!0.25cm!(M)$);
\draw (ja) -- ($(ja)+(jb)-(J)$) -- (jb);
\node[left] at (K) {$K$};
\node[below left] at (L) {$L$};
\node[below right] at (M) {$M$};
\node[above right] at (J) {$J$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The two quadrilaterals are similar; the second has been rotated. Which similarity statement is correct?
